1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Downloading reinvent_pubchem.prior was not a research decision.

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Will this generative starting point cover the chemistry you care about?

3
00:00:45,000 --> 00:01:15,000
If the prior rarely emits your motif, RL wastes its first hours.

4
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Fair test: same Reinvent generator — change only the weights.

5
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:20,000
PubChem prior versus tl_sulfonamide.model after 8 TL epochs.

6
00:02:20,000 --> 00:03:05,000
CPU, seed 42, about 200 SMILES, unique molecules on.

7
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Demo TL: about 13 seconds, peak RAM near 871 MiB.

8
00:03:50,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Sulfonamide hit rate: 8.4% on the prior, 64.3% after TL.

9
00:04:35,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Murcko scaffolds stay high: 168 versus 172. QED is a side effect.

10
00:05:30,000 --> 00:06:10,000
Prior OK? Go to scoring. TL helps? Use it for RL.

11
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:45,000
Need linkers or seed analogues? Switch generator — not more epochs.

12
00:06:45,000 --> 00:07:30,000
Compare, measure, decide — before you burn RL compute.

